• Builder Pattern (Stream.builder() / Static Inner Class)
Constructs immutable objects step-by-step, separating construction logic from representation.

• Lambda Iteration (collection.forEach(item -> ...))
Uses internal iteration where the underlying framework manages the loop execution loop automatically.

• Stream Interface (Stream<T>)
A non-storage pipeline wrapper designed to process sequences of elements lazily.

• Filtering (.filter(Predicate<T>))
An intermediate operation that discards elements that fail a specified condition.

• Method Chaining (.filter().map().sorted())
Combines multiple intermediate transformations into a single, highly readable processing pipeline.

• Parallel Execution (.parallelStream() / .parallel())
Utilizes a Spliterator and ForkJoinPool to split stream chunks across multiple CPU cores.

• Reduction (.reduce(identity, accumulator, combiner))
Folds stream elements down into a single scalar value or custom data structure.

• Decompose & Merge (ForkJoinTask / Combiner)
Forking splits the data structure recursively, while joining merges partial results from different threads.